IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 173D, 173E, 173F, 173G and 173I -- transitional entries in the registers, self-notification by the person, the Registrar's amendment of a register,
-- the transitional rules for contact and residential addresses, and the old records a company keeps.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part sgb2. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
--
-- HOW IT READS. s 173D keeps the particulars lodged before 3 January 2016 in the registers until a notification of change arrives. s 173E has a disqualified director tell the company within 14 days, and lets a person
-- who left office, or changed address, give the Registrar the notice if the company will not. s 173F lets the Registrar amend a register to show a disqualification or a death. s 173G fixes what the Registrar did with
-- alternate, residential and contact addresses from the commencement date. s 173I has a company keep the consent and name-change records of people who were directors or secretaries on 3 January 2016, until they leave office.
-- The commencement dates (of s 66 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025 and of s 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024) are not in the text: they are inputs.

§ `Section 173D: particulars lodged before 3 January 2016`

DECLARE `s 173D(3) the address is entered as` IS ONE OF
    `s 173D(3) the residential address`
    `s 173D(3) the residential address in his or her capacity as chief executive officer of the company`
    `s 173D(3) the auditor's address`

DECLARE `s 173D(3) kind of person lodged` IS ONE OF
    `s 173D(3)(a) a director or a secretary`
    `s 173D(3)(b) a manager`
    `s 173D(3)(c) an auditor`
    `s 173D(3) another person`

-- (1): "In the case of a company incorporated before 3 January 2016 the name and particulars of the persons who were lodged with the Registrar as a director, a secretary or an auditor of the company under section 173
-- in force immediately before that date, must be entered in the company's register of directors, register of secretaries or register of auditors ..., until a notification of any change to the information referred to in
-- section 173(3), (6) or (7) is received by the Registrar under section 173A(1)(b) or (c)."
-- src:15060 | 173D.—(1) In the case of a company incorporated before 3 January
-- src:15061 | 2016 the name and particulars of the persons who were lodged with
-- src:15062 | the Registrar as a director, a secretary or an auditor of the company
-- src:15063 | under section 173 in force immediately before that date, must be
-- src:15064 | entered in the company’s register of directors, register of secretaries
-- src:15065 | or register of auditors (whichever may be applicable) referred to in
-- src:15066 | section 173, until a notification of any change to the information
-- src:15067 | referred to in section 173(3), (6) or (7) is received by the Registrar
-- src:15068 | under section 173A(1)(b) or (c).
@ref s 173D(1) (src:15060-15068)
GIVEN `the day the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the person was lodged with the Registrar as a director, a secretary or an auditor of the company under section 173 in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification of a change to the information referred to in section 173(3), (6) or (7) has been received by the Registrar under section 173A(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173D(1) the name and particulars must remain entered in the register of directors, secretaries or auditors` MEANS
    IF (`the day the company was incorporated` AT LEAST (Date 3 1 2016)) OR (NOT `the person was lodged with the Registrar as a director, a secretary or an auditor of the company under section 173 in force immediately before 3 January 2016`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company incorporated before 3 January 2016 the name and particulars of the persons who were lodged ..." limits the subsection to those companies and persons, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF `a notification of a change to the information referred to in section 173(3), (6) or (7) has been received by the Registrar under section 173A(1)(b) or (c)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be entered ... until a notification of any change ... is received by the Registrar under section 173A(1)(b) or (c)" (an "until" once met: the Guide's "In short" line)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2): the same for managers, whose name and particulars go into the register of chief executive officers, until a notification of change in the information in s 173(5) is received.
-- src:15074 | (2) Where a company mentioned in subsection (1) has lodged the
-- src:15075 | name and particulars of one or more managers with the Registrar as a
-- src:15076 | manager or managers (as the case may be) of the company under
-- src:15077 | section 173 in force immediately before 3 January 2016, the name
-- src:15078 | and particulars of the manager or managers (as the case may be) must
-- src:15079 | be entered in the company’s register of chief executive officers
-- src:15080 | referred to in section 173, until a notification of any change in the
-- src:15081 | information referred to in section 173(5) is received by the Registrar
-- src:15082 | under section 173A(1)(b) or (c).
@ref s 173D(2) (src:15074-15082)
GIVEN `the day the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the company had lodged the name and particulars of the person with the Registrar as a manager of the company under section 173 in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification of a change in the information referred to in section 173(5) has been received by the Registrar under section 173A(1)(b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173D(2) the name and particulars of the manager must remain entered in the register of chief executive officers` MEANS
    IF (`the day the company was incorporated` AT LEAST (Date 3 1 2016)) OR (NOT `the company had lodged the name and particulars of the person with the Registrar as a manager of the company under section 173 in force immediately before 3 January 2016`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company mentioned in subsection (1) has lodged the name and particulars of one or more managers" limits the subsection to those companies and managers, with no "only"
    ELSE IF `a notification of a change in the information referred to in section 173(5) has been received by the Registrar under section 173A(1)(b) or (c)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be entered in the company's register of chief executive officers ..., until a notification of any change ... is received" (an "until" once met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (3): "(a) the address lodged ... in respect of any director or secretary ... must be entered as his or her residential address; (b) the address lodged ... in respect of any manager ... must be entered as his or her
-- residential address in his or her capacity as chief executive officer of the company; and (c) the address lodged ... in respect of any auditor ... must be entered as the auditor's address."
-- src:15088 | (3) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2) —
-- src:15090 | (a) the address lodged with the Registrar in respect of any
-- src:15091 | director or secretary under section 173 in force
-- src:15096 | immediately before 3 January 2016 must be entered as his
-- src:15097 | or her residential address;
-- src:15099 | (b) the address lodged with the Registrar in respect of any
-- src:15100 | manager under section 173 in force immediately before
-- src:15101 | 3 January 2016 must be entered as his or her residential
-- src:15102 | address in his or her capacity as chief executive officer of
-- src:15103 | the company; and
-- src:15105 | (c) the address lodged with the Registrar in respect of any
-- src:15106 | auditor under section 173 in force immediately before
-- src:15107 | 3 January 2016, must be entered as the auditor’s address.
@ref s 173D(3) (src:15088-15107)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 173D(3) kind of person lodged`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 173D(3) the address is entered as`
`s 173D(3) the address lodged is to be entered as` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 173D(3)(a) a director or a secretary` THEN JUST `s 173D(3) the residential address`
    WHEN `s 173D(3)(b) a manager` THEN JUST `s 173D(3) the residential address in his or her capacity as chief executive officer of the company`
    WHEN `s 173D(3)(c) an auditor` THEN JUST `s 173D(3) the auditor's address`
    WHEN `s 173D(3) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2)" names directors, secretaries, managers and auditors, and says nothing of another person

§ `Section 173E: self-notification`

DECLARE `s 173E act` IS ONE OF
    `s 173E(1)(a) notify the company of the director's disqualification`

-- (1): "A director who ceases on or after the date of commencement of section 66 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025 to be qualified to act as a director by virtue of section 148(1), 154(1), 155(1),
-- 155A(1), 155C(1) or 155D(1), or by a disqualification order made by the Court under section 149, 149A or 154(2) (a) must, without affecting section 165(1)(c), notify the company of his or her disqualification as soon as
-- practicable but not later than 14 days after the disqualification".
-- src:15115 | 173E.—(1) A director who ceases on or after the date of
-- src:15116 | commencement of section 66 of the Corporate and Accounting
-- src:15117 | Laws (Amendment) Act 2025 to be qualified to act as a director by
-- src:15118 | virtue of section 148(1), 154(1), 155(1), 155A(1), 155C(1) or
-- src:15119 | 155D(1), or by a disqualification order made by the Court under
-- src:15120 | section 149, 149A or 154(2) —
-- src:15122 | (a) must, without affecting section 165(1)(c), notify the
-- src:15123 | company of his or her disqualification as soon as
-- src:15124 | practicable but not later than 14 days after the
-- src:15125 | disqualification; and
@ref s 173E(1) (src:15115-15125)
GIVEN `the day the director ceased to be qualified to act as a director by virtue of a provision or order the subsection names` IS A DATE
      `the day the section 66 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025 commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the director notified the company of the disqualification` IS A DATE
      `the director notified the company as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173E(1)(a) the director notified the company of the disqualification in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the director ceased to be qualified to act as a director by virtue of a provision or order the subsection names` LESS THAN `the day the section 66 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025 commenced`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A director who ceases on or after the date of commencement of section 66 ... to be qualified" limits the duty to that time, with no "only" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF `the director notified the company as soon as practicable` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the director ceased to be qualified to act as a director by virtue of a provision or order the subsection names` `the day the director notified the company of the disqualification` 14 Days
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must ... notify the company of his or her disqualification as soon as practicable but not later than 14 days after the disqualification" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:15122 | (a) must, without affecting section 165(1)(c), notify the
-- src:15123 | company of his or her disqualification as soon as
-- src:15124 | practicable but not later than 14 days after the
-- src:15125 | disqualification; and
@ref s 173E(1)(a) (src:15122-15125)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 173E act`
`s 173E(1)(a) the director must notify the company of the disqualification within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 173E(1)(a) notify the company of the director's disqualification`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not notify the company of his or her disqualification within 14 days after the disqualification"

-- (1)(b): "may give the notice mentioned in section 173A(1)(b), (c) or (d) to the Registrar if the director has reasonable cause to believe that the company will not do so". A power whose "if" gate failed answers
-- NOTHING (limit 1 of the ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-173E-1).
-- src:15127 | (b) may give the notice mentioned in section 173A(1)(b), (c)
-- src:15128 | or (d) to the Registrar if the director has reasonable cause to
-- src:15129 | believe that the company will not do so.
@ref s 173E(1)(b) (src:15127-15129)
GIVEN `the director ceased on or after the commencement of section 66 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025 to be qualified to act as a director by virtue of a provision or order the subsection names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has reasonable cause to believe that the company will not give the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173E(1)(b) the director may give the notice to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the director ceased on or after the commencement of section 66 of the Corporate and Accounting Laws (Amendment) Act 2025 to be qualified to act as a director by virtue of a provision or order the subsection names` AND `the director has reasonable cause to believe that the company will not give the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (grant): a function named for a power ("may give the notice") whose "if" gate failed answers NOTHING, with a fork line: limit 1 of the ruling of 2026-11-12 (fork F-173E-1 in NOTES.md)

DECLARE `s 173E kind of person who may give the notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 173E(2) a director who resigns from office and has given notice of his or her resignation to the company`
    `s 173E(2) a director who is removed or retires from office`
    `s 173E(3) a secretary who resigns from office and has given notice of his or her resignation to the company`
    `s 173E(3) a secretary who is removed or retires from office`
    `s 173E(4) a director, chief executive officer or secretary who has changed his or her residential address or contact address, or an auditor who has changed the auditor's address`
    `s 173E another person`

-- (2): a director who resigns (having given notice) or is removed or retires "may give the notice referred to in section 173A(1)(b) to the Registrar if the director has reasonable cause to believe that the company will not
-- do so". (3): the same for a secretary. (4): a director, chief executive officer or secretary who has changed an address entered in the register, or an auditor who has changed the auditor's address, "may give the notice
-- referred to in section 173A(1)(c) ... if he or she has reasonable cause to believe that the company will not do so".
