-- src:15159 | section 173, may give the notice referred to in section 173A(1)(c) to
-- src:15160 | the Registrar if he or she has reasonable cause to believe that the
-- src:15161 | company will not do so.
@ref s 173E(4) (src:15153-15161)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 173E kind of person who may give the notice`
      `the person has reasonable cause to believe that the company will not give the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173E the person may give the notice to the Registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 173E another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsections (2) to (4) name the persons who may give the notice and say nothing of another person
    OTHERWISE
        (IF `the person has reasonable cause to believe that the company will not give the notice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (grant): a function named for a power ("may give the notice") whose "if" gate failed answers NOTHING, with a fork line: limit 1 of the ruling of 2026-11-12 (fork F-173E-1 in NOTES.md)

§ `Section 173F: amendment of a register by the Registrar`

DECLARE `s 173F kind of belief` IS ONE OF
    `s 173F(1) a director of the company has been disqualified from being or acting as a director`
    `s 173F(1A) a director of the company is dead`
    `s 173F(2) a chief executive officer of the company is dead`
    `s 173F(3) a secretary of the company is dead`
    `s 173F(4)(a) the auditor has had its registration as an accounting entity suspended or removed`
    `s 173F(4)(b) the auditor, being an individual, is dead`
    `s 173F(5) the Registrar made an amendment under subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3) or (4) under a mistaken belief that the person had ceased to be director, chief executive officer, secretary or auditor`
    `s 173F another case`

-- (1) to (5): "Where the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that [the fact], the Registrar may on his or her own initiative amend the register ... to indicate [the effect]". The six subsections have one shape and one
-- answer, so one function carries them (split site (ii): a "may" gated by "Where"; fork F-173F-1 in NOTES.md).
