-- src:15226 | indicate that the person has ceased to be an auditor of the company by
-- src:15227 | virtue of that fact.
@ref s 173F(4) (src:15216-15227)
-- src:15231 | (5) Where the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe that he or
-- src:15232 | she has made an amendment to the relevant register under
-- src:15233 | subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3) or (4) under a mistaken belief that a
-- src:15234 | director, a chief executive officer, a secretary or an auditor (as the
-- src:15235 | case may be) of a company has ceased to be a director, a chief
-- src:15236 | executive officer, a secretary or an auditor (as the case may be) of the
-- src:15237 | company, the Registrar may on his or her own initiative amend the
-- src:15238 | register of directors, register of chief executive officers, register of
-- src:15239 | secretaries or register of auditors to restore the name of the person in
-- src:15240 | such register.
@ref s 173F(5) (src:15231-15240)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 173F kind of belief`
      `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe the fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173F the Registrar may on his or her own initiative amend the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 173F another case` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section names six cases and says nothing of another
    OTHERWISE
        (IF `the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe the fact`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (grant): the Registrar's power is limited by "Where the Registrar has reasonable cause to believe" in its own wording, and the case falls outside the limit (the grant rule of section 5 of the Guide; split site (ii): the other reading is JUST FALSE under the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

§ `Section 173G: the transitional rules for contact and residential addresses`

-- The commencement date is "the date of commencement of section 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024" (subsection (6)), which the text does not state: an input.
-- src:15336 | (6) In this section, “commencement date” means the date of
-- src:15337 | commencement of section 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory
-- src:15338 | Enhancements) Act 2024.
@ref s 173G(6) (src:15336-15338)
GIVEN `the day the section 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024 commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173G(6) the day is the commencement date` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` EQUALS `the day the section 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024 commenced`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“commencement date” means the date of commencement of section 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024" (a "means" definition)

-- (1): "Where, immediately before the commencement date, there is an alternate address of a director, chief executive officer or secretary entered in the register ..., the Registrar must, as from that date, cause (a) the
-- alternate address to be kept as the contact address ... instead of as the alternate address ..., until notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged under any ACRA administered Act on or after that date".
