-- src:15275 | officer or secretary entered in the register of directors,
-- src:15276 | register of chief executive officers or register of secretaries
-- src:15277 | (as the case may be) of a company kept by the Registrar
-- src:15278 | under section 173(1)(a), (b) or (c), respectively; and
-- src:15280 | (b) the residential address of the director, chief executive
-- src:15281 | officer or secretary is entered in the register of directors,
-- src:15282 | register of chief executive officers or register of secretaries
-- src:15283 | (as the case may be) of the company,
-- src:15285 | the Registrar must, as from the commencement date, cause —
-- src:15287 | (c) the residential address to be kept as the contact address of
-- src:15288 | that director, chief executive officer or secretary in that
-- src:15289 | register until notice of a change in the individual’s contact
-- src:15290 | address is lodged under any ACRA administered Act on or
-- src:15291 | after that date, in addition to being kept as the residential
-- src:15296 | address of that director, chief executive officer or
-- src:15297 | secretary; and
-- src:15299 | (d) the contact address to be made available for public access
-- src:15300 | under section 12(2)(c) as the address of that director, chief
-- src:15301 | executive officer or secretary.
@ref s 173G(2) (src:15272-15301)
GIVEN `immediately before the commencement date there is no alternate address of the director, chief executive officer or secretary entered in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement date the residential address of the director, chief executive officer or secretary is entered in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under an ACRA administered Act on or after the commencement date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173G(2)(c) the Registrar must keep the residential address as the contact address as well` MEANS
    IF (NOT `immediately before the commencement date there is no alternate address of the director, chief executive officer or secretary entered in the register`) OR (NOT `immediately before the commencement date the residential address of the director, chief executive officer or secretary is entered in the register`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, immediately before the commencement date (a) there is no alternate address ...; and (b) the residential address ... is entered ..., the Registrar must, as from the commencement date, cause" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-173G-1)
    ELSE IF `notice of a change in the individual's contact address has been lodged under an ACRA administered Act on or after the commencement date`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "kept as the contact address ... until notice of a change in the individual's contact address is lodged" (an "until" once met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:15299 | (d) the contact address to be made available for public access
-- src:15300 | under section 12(2)(c) as the address of that director, chief
-- src:15301 | executive officer or secretary.
@ref s 173G(2) (src:15299-15301)
GIVEN `immediately before the commencement date there is no alternate address of the director, chief executive officer or secretary entered in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before the commencement date the residential address of the director, chief executive officer or secretary is entered in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173G(2)(d) the Registrar must make the contact address available for public access` MEANS
    IF `immediately before the commencement date there is no alternate address of the director, chief executive officer or secretary entered in the register` AND `immediately before the commencement date the residential address of the director, chief executive officer or secretary is entered in the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... (a) there is no alternate address ...; and (b) the residential address ... is entered ... the Registrar must ... cause ... (d) the contact address to be made available for public access" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-173G-1)

-- (3): "Where (a) before the commencement date, the residential address of a director, chief executive officer or secretary of a company (called in this subsection the individual) has been entered in the register ...; and
-- (b) on the commencement date, those registers do not show that the individual holds any of the positions mentioned in paragraph (a) in the same company, the Registrar must, as from the commencement date, cause
-- the individual's residential address to be excluded from public access to that register of that company under section 12(2)(c)."
-- src:15305 | (3) Where —
-- src:15307 | (a) before the commencement date, the residential address of a
-- src:15308 | director, chief executive officer or secretary of a company
-- src:15309 | (called in this subsection the individual) has been entered
-- src:15310 | in the register of directors, register of chief executive
-- src:15311 | officers or register of secretaries, of the company; and
-- src:15313 | (b) on the commencement date, those registers do not show
-- src:15314 | that the individual holds any of the positions mentioned in
-- src:15315 | paragraph (a) in the same company,
-- src:15317 | the Registrar must, as from the commencement date, cause the
-- src:15318 | individual’s residential address to be excluded from public access to
-- src:15319 | that register of that company under section 12(2)(c).
@ref s 173G(3) (src:15305-15319)
GIVEN `before the commencement date the residential address of the individual has been entered in the register of directors, chief executive officers or secretaries of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the commencement date those registers do not show that the individual holds any of those positions in the same company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173G(3) the Registrar must exclude the individual's residential address from public access` MEANS
    IF `before the commencement date the residential address of the individual has been entered in the register of directors, chief executive officers or secretaries of the company` AND `on the commencement date those registers do not show that the individual holds any of those positions in the same company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where (a) ... and (b) ..., the Registrar must, as from the commencement date, cause the individual's residential address to be excluded from public access" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-173G-1)

-- (4) and (5): a notice or information under s 173A or 173B about an appointment or change before the commencement date, furnished on or after that date, must provide the information required by s 173 as in force when it is furnished.
-- src:15323 | (4) Subsection (5) applies to a notice or information required to be
-- src:15324 | furnished or given under section 173A or 173B (as the case may be)
-- src:15325 | relating to an appointment or change in the appointment of a director,
-- src:15326 | chief executive officer or secretary of a company which occurred
-- src:15327 | before the commencement date.
@ref s 173G(4) (src:15323-15327)
-- src:15329 | (5) Where the notice or information mentioned in subsection (4) is
-- src:15330 | furnished or given on or after the commencement date, the notice or
-- src:15331 | information must provide the information required under section 173
-- src:15332 | as in force when the notice or information is furnished or given,
-- src:15333 | despite the appointment or the change in the appointment having
-- src:15334 | occurred before the commencement date.
@ref s 173G(5) (src:15329-15334)
GIVEN `the day of the appointment or change in the appointment` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice or information is furnished or given` IS A DATE
      `the day the section 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024 commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173G(5) the notice or information must provide the information required under section 173 as in force when it is furnished` MEANS
    IF `the day of the appointment or change in the appointment` AT LEAST `the day the section 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024 commenced`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) applies "to a notice or information ... relating to an appointment or change ... which occurred before the commencement date" and the text says nothing of a later appointment
    ELSE IF `the day the notice or information is furnished or given` AT LEAST `the day the section 40 of the ACRA (Registry and Regulatory Enhancements) Act 2024 commenced`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the notice or information mentioned in subsection (4) is furnished or given on or after the commencement date, the notice or information must provide the information required under section 173 as in force when" it is furnished (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-173G-1)

§ `Section 173I: old records a company keeps`

DECLARE `s 173I kind of record` IS ONE OF
    `s 173I(1)(a)(i) the signed copy of the person's consent to act as a director mentioned in section 173(2)(a) in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
    `s 173I(1)(a)(ii) documentary evidence (if any) of any change in the person's name mentioned in section 173(2)(c) in force immediately before that date`
    `s 173I(1)(b) the signed copy of the person's consent to act as a secretary mentioned in section 173(4A) in force immediately before that date`
    `s 173I some other record`

DECLARE `s 173I act` IS ONE OF
    `s 173I(1) continue to keep the old consents and evidence of change of name`

-- (1) and (2): "A company must continue to keep the following information for the periods set out in subsection (2)": for each person who is a director (or secretary) immediately before 3 January 2016, the consent
-- (and any evidence of change of name). "The period ... commences on 3 January 2016 and ceases on (a) ... the date on which the person ceases to be a director of the company; or (b) ... a secretary".
-- src:15369 | 173I.—(1) A company must continue to keep the following
-- src:15370 | information for the periods set out in subsection (2):
-- src:15372 | (a) with respect to each person who is a director of the
-- src:15373 | company immediately before 3 January 2016 —
-- src:15375 | (i) the signed copy of the person’s consent to act as a
-- src:15376 | director mentioned in section 173(2)(a) in force
-- src:15377 | immediately before that date; and
-- src:15379 | (ii) documentary evidence (if any) of any change in the
-- src:15380 | person’s name mentioned in section 173(2)(c) in
-- src:15381 | force immediately before that date;
-- src:15383 | (b) with respect to each person who is a secretary of the
-- src:15384 | company immediately before 3 January 2016, the signed
-- src:15385 | copy of the person’s consent to act as a secretary
-- src:15386 | mentioned in section 173(4A) in force immediately
-- src:15387 | before that date.
@ref s 173I(1) (src:15369-15387)
-- src:15391 | (2) The period mentioned in subsection (1) commences on
-- src:15392 | 3 January 2016 and ceases on —
-- src:15397 | (a) in the case of subsection (1)(a), the date on which the
-- src:15398 | person ceases to be a director of the company; or
-- src:15400 | (b) in the case of subsection (1)(b), the date on which the
-- src:15401 | person ceases to be a secretary of the company.
@ref s 173I(2) (src:15391-15401)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 173I kind of record`
      `the person was a director (for paragraph (a)) or a secretary (for paragraph (b)) of the company immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is documentary evidence of a change in the person's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has ceased to be a director or secretary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person ceased to be a director or secretary of the company` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173I the company must continue to keep the record on the day` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person was a director (for paragraph (a)) or a secretary (for paragraph (b)) of the company immediately before 3 January 2016`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with respect to each person who is a director of the company immediately before 3 January 2016" (and "secretary") limits the duty to those persons, with no "only"
    ELSE IF `the day in question` LESS THAN (Date 3 1 2016)
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "The period ... commences on 3 January 2016" and the subsection says nothing of an earlier day
         ELSE CONSIDER kind
              WHEN `s 173I some other record` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): subsection (1) names three records without "only"
              OTHERWISE
                  (IF (kind EQUALS `s 173I(1)(a)(ii) documentary evidence (if any) of any change in the person's name mentioned in section 173(2)(c) in force immediately before that date`) AND (NOT `there is documentary evidence of a change in the person's name`)
                   THEN JUST TRUE   -- the paragraph asks for the evidence "(if any)": with none, there is nothing to keep
                   ELSE (IF `the person has ceased to be a director or secretary of the company` AND `the day in question` GREATER THAN `the day the person ceased to be a director or secretary of the company`
                         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The period mentioned in subsection (1) commences on 3 January 2016 and ceases on ... the date on which the person ceases to be a director of the company" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
                         ELSE JUST TRUE))

-- The duty is a continuing "must continue to keep" with no time: no breach path ("Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md).
-- src:15369 | 173I.—(1) A company must continue to keep the following
-- src:15370 | information for the periods set out in subsection (2):
@ref s 173I(1) (src:15369-15370)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 173I act`
`s 173I(1) the company must continue to keep the old consents and evidence of change of name` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 173I(1) continue to keep the old consents and evidence of change of name`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:15405 | (3) Section 173(8) in force immediately before 3 January 2016
-- src:15406 | continues to apply in respect of any information lodged with the
-- src:15407 | Registrar under section 173 in force immediately before that date.
@ref s 173I(3) (src:15405-15407)
GIVEN `the information was lodged with the Registrar under section 173 in force immediately before 3 January 2016` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173I(3) section 173(8) as in force immediately before 3 January 2016 continues to apply to the information` MEANS
    IF `the information was lodged with the Registrar under section 173 in force immediately before 3 January 2016`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 173(8) in force immediately before 3 January 2016 continues to apply in respect of any information lodged with the Registrar under section 173 in force immediately before that date" limits the continuation to that information
